<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi was hoping someone can help, I have MD-9600 {M1-V4A} GPS 2205 on the main board, would this be AES compatible? I can program AES keys over to the radio and it comes up with the encryption logo in the radio but it's not encrypting the audio, so I am either doing something wrong or the radio is not compatible?<br><br>Hardware version = 02.09<br>MCU = S026.045<br><br>Thank you</div></blockquote>This forum is dedicated to the OpenGD77 firmware which does not support any form of encryption becuase its totally illegal for Ham radio use.<br><br>The OpenGD77 firmware will never include encryption because even to add it to the firmware would be a legal nightmare for the developers.<br><br>So you won't find the answer to that question here.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Dec 09, 2024 10:27 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
